                <pb facs="0568" n="458" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg458"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/5300: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chairman of the American Delegation to the Sixth International
                        Conference of American States</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hughes</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-01-28T15:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 28,
                                1928—3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>32. For Mr. Francis White. Text of new draft of proposed electoral law thoroughly
                    satisfactory to Department and to Dodds.</p>
                <p>It appears that the words “or <hi rendition="#italic">suplente</hi>” after
                    “political members” and before “if for any reason” in penultimate sentence of
                    Article 2 may have been omitted through oversight. Department does not consider
                    this point important.</p>
                <p>Above repeated to Managua.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
